    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="1048" n="1034" xml:id="pg1034"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/5637: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-17T18:00:00+03:00">April 17, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 18—2:31 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1326. Reference my 1020, March 24, 6 p.m., and 1083, March 28, 1 p.m.<anchor
                        n="96" xml:id="d591-f1"/> A memorandum has been received from the Foreign
                    Office in reply to my memorandum of March 21 regarding the creation of the War
                    Refugee Board which states in substance that the policy of the Soviet Government
                    has been, and still is, to give assistance of every kind to the victims of
                    persecution by Hitlerite Germany. In keeping with this principle, the Soviet
                    Government has agreed to the passage of a Turkish vessel and three Bulgarian
                    ships from Rumanian and Bulgarian ports to Turkey for the purpose of evacuating
                    refugees, as the Embassy already knows.</p>
                <p>I plan to discuss with the Foreign Office the possibility of further Soviet
                    cooperation in the implementation of our policy at the first favorable
                    opportunity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
